# WS5-05/06/08 (cleanup after a runtime fault), A1200/KS3.1 under FS-UAE
# (54x-fs-uae.sh case 541). Sources: exec.library autodocs (AddIntServer: the server
# must be removed with RemIntServer before its code or Interrupt structure goes away;
# a public port must be removed before its memory is freed); spec/05-statements.md §15
# and spec/11-memory.md (a runtime fault aborts the program without the cleanup
# ladder); spec/appendix-amiga.md (the shim owns the OS-level resources). The
# language rule and the platform rule together require the fault exit to leave no OS
# registration pointing into the unloaded program.
# Expected: the fault line, rc 20, and an after line equal to the before line
# (vertb N, port 0); the machine keeps running to END.
# Contrast 541c (pick(1), no fault): prints 2, removes the handler and the port, and
# the walker lines are equal.
# Detector: the walker reports vertb N+1 and port 1 after 54x-seeded.c.
expect: script
--- output
before vertb N port 0 card 1
armed
error E11211: index out of range
rc 20
after vertb N port 0 card 1
END
